.TH MYCAT 3 "November 2026" "libmyutils 0.4.1" "libmyutils Manual"
.SH NAME
mycat \- print the contents of a file to standard output
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <myfilefunctions.h>
.sp
.BI "int mycat(const char *" filename );
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B mycat
function opens the file named by
.I filename
for reading and writes its entire contents to
.I stdout
in fixed-size buffered chunks, similar in spirit to the
.BR cat (1)
utility.
.PP
If
.I filename
is
.B NULL
or the file cannot be opened, an error is reported via
.BR perror (3)
and the function fails.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns 0 on success.
Returns \-1 if
.I filename
is
.B NULL
or the file could not be opened.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
#include <myfilefunctions.h>

int main(void) {
    if (mycat("notes.txt") != 0)
        return 1;
    return 0;
}
.fi
.SH AUTHOR
Written as part of the OS Assignment 01: Core C Utilities Library.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cat (1),
.BR mygrep (3),
.BR myfile_stats (3)
